.Dd November 22, 2026
.Dt COMPASS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm compass
.Nd run a simulated system by hand and save the run; the Criticality Compass rulebook commands
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm hold
.Fl -list
.Nm
.Cm hold
.Op Fl -dry
.Fl -needle Ar MODE
.Op Fl -seed Ar N
.Op Fl -wall Ar SECONDS
.Op Fl -out Ar DIR
.Ar system Ar world
.Nm
.Cm hold
.Fl -verify Ar RECORD
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
.Cm hold
runs one hold of a catalogue system.
A needle steers a dial on a simulated system that is served over the apparatus wire,
and the run is scored against the truth the server keeps.
The command prints the input it resolved, one
.Dq RUN
line per step, and the scored output, and it saves the run as a record:
a directory with the files the run read, the files it wrote, and a manifest of their sha256 values.
.Pp
.Ar system
is a catalogue system and
.Ar world
is either one of its catalogue world names or the path of a world file ending in
.Pa .toml .
No hold mode is the default.
A run with no
.Fl -needle
is refused (exit 2) and the message names the needles the system has.
.Pp
The command wraps
.Dq python -m environment.run_hold
and changes nothing in it.
A run needs numpy and scipy, and the wheel declares both.
.Sh INSTALL
Build the wheel from a clone and install it into a fresh virtual environment; pip brings numpy and scipy:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ python3 -m pip wheel --no-deps --no-build-isolation -w dist .
$ python3 -m venv hold-venv
$ hold-venv/bin/python -m pip install dist/criticality_compass-*.whl
$ hold-venv/bin/compass hold --list
.Ed
.Pp
The wheel carries the catalogue, the systems and the apparatus files, and installs this manual page as
.Pa share/man/man1/compass.1
under the environment's prefix.
Outside a clone a record's git line reads
.Dq not-a-clone .
.Sh CATALOGUE
.Nm
.Cm hold
.Fl -list
prints one line per world:
the system, the world name, the needles that world accepts, and the world file.
Ising has the worlds production, static, static-r2, static-r3, field and field-hard.
AT has production and static.
FHN is listed as pending and cannot be run.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -needle Ar MODE
The hold mode: a catalogue needle name or the path of a needle
.Pa .toml
file.
Required for a run.
.It Fl -seed Ar N
The one override.
The command writes a copy of the world with this seed and runs the copy;
the record says the seed was overridden.
.It Fl -wall Ar SECONDS
Wall-clock limit in seconds, greater than 0, 1800 by default.
At the limit the run is stopped, nothing is left listening on its port, a record is still written, and the exit status is 3.
.It Fl -out Ar DIR
Where records go.
The default is
.Ev COMPASS_RUNS
if it is set, else
.Pa ./compass-runs
under the directory you ran in.
.It Fl -dry
Print the resolved input and write nothing.
.It Fl -list
Print the catalogue.
.It Fl -verify Ar RECORD
Recompute every hash a record lists.
It names each file that is missing, differs, or is in the record but not listed in
.Pa run.json ,
and exits 1; otherwise it prints "verified: every file matches run.json" and exits 0.
A
.Pa run.json
that lists no outputs is refused (exit 2).
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev COMPASS_RUNS
The directory records go to when
.Fl -out
is not given.
.El
.Sh FILES
A record is the directory
.Pa <UTC time>-<system>-<world>-<run id>-<4 hex>
under the output directory.
Every path in it is relative to the record.
Two identical runs leave two records.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa run.json
The manifest, with sorted keys:
argv, exit, finished_utc, inputs, needle, orchestrator_exit, outputs, port, record, run_id, schema, seed, seed_overridden, started_utc, status, summary, system, versions, wall_limit_s, wall_s, world.
.Va versions
holds compass, git (head and dirty, or not-a-clone), code_digest, python, numpy and platform.
.Va outputs
lists every other file in the record with its sha256 and size.
.It Pa run.json.sha256
The sha256 of
.Pa run.json .
.It Pa terminal.txt
What the command printed.
.It Pa input/
The env, world, needle and score files the run read, and the tau file beside the world when the system has one.
.It Pa run/
What the orchestrator wrote:
config.json, report.jsonl, map.jsonl, truth.json, score.json, map-truth.json, server.log, perf.json and edge.json for a scored run; refused.json for a refused one.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It 0
scored: the run finished and
.Pa run/score.json
was written, whatever the outcome.
.It 1
infrastructure-failure: the run could not be carried out.
An exit code of the orchestrator that this table does not hold is recorded as unknown-exit and also exits 1.
.It 2
refused: the run was refused before it started (no needle named, a world file with no top-level seed, a system with no tau file), no arguments were given (the usage is printed), or
.Fl -verify
was given a run.json that lists no outputs.
.It 3
wall-clock: the wall-clock limit stopped the run.
.It 64
usage-error: an option or argument the command does not take, or a
.Fl -wall
that is not greater than 0.
.El
.Pp
.Fl -verify
exits 0 when the record is as it was written and 1 when it is not.
.Sh EXAMPLES
List the catalogue:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ compass hold --list
ising  production  needles: settled mid settled-off   (system-instantiated/plugins/ising/ising-apparatus.toml)
ising  static      needles: settled mid settled-off   (system-instantiated/plugins/ising/ising-apparatus-static.toml)
ising  static-r2   needles: settled mid settled-off   (system-instantiated/plugins/ising/ising-apparatus-static-r2.toml)
ising  static-r3   needles: settled mid settled-off   (system-instantiated/plugins/ising/ising-apparatus-static-r3.toml)
ising  field       needles: settled mid settled-off   (system-instantiated/plugins/ising/ising-apparatus-field.toml)
ising  field-hard  needles: settled mid settled-off   (system-instantiated/plugins/ising/ising-apparatus-field-hard.toml)
at     production  needles: settled mid settled-off mid-off mid-null   (system-instantiated/plugins/at/at-apparatus.toml)
at     static      needles: settled mid settled-off mid-off mid-null   (system-instantiated/plugins/at/at-apparatus-static.toml)
fhn    pending     not in this release
.Ed
.Pp
Look at what a run would read, and write nothing:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ compass hold --dry ising production --needle settled
INPUT
  system ising  world production  needle settled  seed 500 (from the world file)
  world  system-instantiated/plugins/ising/ising-apparatus.toml  sha256 93587cb627b5
…
  needle needle-settings/ising/hold-settled.toml  sha256 c2159cac0b3e
  needle params: needle_structure=hold-pair-v1 g=12 step=6 S=1500 n_eq=450
  score  environment/hold-score-ising.toml  sha256 158dbcc14f0e
dry run: nothing written
.Ed
.Pp
Run it.
The lines marked with an ellipsis are left out here; the run printed 53 RUN lines.
In the OUTPUT line,
.Dv HORIZON
means the run reached its horizon, lock=
.Dv HELD
that the lock was held at the end (
.Dv LOST
if it was not), and in_fraction the share of the hold steps inside the window.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ compass hold ising production --needle settled
INPUT
  system ising  world production  needle settled  seed 500 (from the world file)
  world  system-instantiated/plugins/ising/ising-apparatus.toml  sha256 93587cb627b5
  needle needle-settings/ising/hold-settled.toml  sha256 c2159cac0b3e
  needle params: needle_structure=hold-pair-v1 g=12 step=6 S=1500 n_eq=450
  score  environment/hold-score-ising.toml  sha256 158dbcc14f0e
  score params: offset_K=-0.005 out_run=3 plan=1569
  code   compass 1.0.0a0  git 729f1ae0238e  digest 9eaa1dcbf166
RUN step 1 phase ignite index 5100  t=10s
…
RUN step 53 phase hold index 198426  t=284s
OUTPUT
  outcome=HORIZON lock=HELD in_fraction=0.9583333333333334 rms_e_g=0.48005523022349245 mean_e=-4.748954039085869 hold_steps=48 accuracy=0.5625  run_id=0811b05bffd7880d
record: 20261122T001603Z-ising-production-0811b05bffd7880d-0622
exit 0: scored  (status scored)
.Ed
.Pp
Check the record:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ compass hold --verify compass-runs/<record>
.Ed
.Sh COST
A run is minutes of compute.
Measured here, one run at a time, at nice 19, on an 8-core machine.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ising production, needle settled
284 s, at 1-minute load 13.0 at the start and 8.6 at the end.
.It AT production, needle settled
501 s, at 1-minute load 2.7 at the start and 11.0 at the end.
.El
.Pp
A short test world with horizon 1 finishes in about 2 s.
.Sh KNOWN FINDINGS
In the static worlds the needle can enter its hold before its pair of points brackets the crossing (seed 533).
.Sh THE RULEBOOK COMMANDS
.Nm
with any other command runs the rulebook command line (help, show, explain, run, validate, tables, new, tabulate, family, and the rest).
It is a second surface of the same tool and is unchanged.
.Nm
.Cm help
lists the basic commands and
.Nm
.Cm help
.Fl -advanced
lists all of them.
The commands run, check and freeze need the external structure checker named by
.Ev CC_STRUCTURE_CHECKS
and refuse without it.
.Sh SEE ALSO
README.md (Run a system by hand), docs/ARCHITECTURE.md (The hold path).
